# 11. Access Specifiers

C++ has:

```text
public
private
protected
```

### Public

Accessible from anywhere.

```cpp
class A {
public:
    int x;
};
```

```cpp
A obj;
obj.x = 10; // ✅
```

### Private

Accessible only inside the class.

```cpp
class A {
private:
    int x;
};
```

```cpp
obj.x = 10; // ❌
```

### Protected

Accessible inside the class and derived classes.

```cpp
class A {
protected:
    int x;
};

class B : public A {
public:
    void test() {
        x = 10; // ✅
    }
};
```

